    "optionsVersion": 1,
    "apiVersion": "VERSION_0",
    "isResourceIntensiveScript": false,
    "showPartitioning": false,
    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Finds the k nearest points in a second input for each point in the first, by great-circle distance, with an optional distance limit and a catchment summary per destination.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Geo",
    "tags": [
        "nearest",
        "distance",
        "spatial",
        "geo",
        "catchment",
        "latitude",
        "longitude",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "For each point in the **first input** (customers, properties, incidents, vehicles) finds the **nearest points in the second input** (stores, branches, depots, engineers, competitors) by straight-line (great-circle) distance on the earth's surface.\n\n- **k nearest**: the single nearest, or the nearest 3, 5 or more, each with its rank\n- **Maximum distance**: only matches within, say, 25 km; points with nothing in range are kept and marked *None within distance* (or dropped)\n- Distance in **kilometres or miles**, plus the **bearing** and compass **direction** from the point to its match\n- All fields of the matched destination are appended (prefixed *Nearest:*)\n- A second output gives a **catchment summary** per destination: how many points have it as their nearest, mean, median and furthest distance, share of points\n\nLatitude and longitude in decimal degrees (WGS84). Pure numpy: fine for hundreds of thousands of points against thousands of destinations.",
    "dependencies": "",
